  "description_html": "Restoration of <i>Sinovenator</i> (Dinosauria; Theropoda; Coelurosauria; Troodontidae). My original restoration of <i>Sinovenator</i> (uploaded in 2009) was based on the holotype IVPP V12615.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Xu_et.al._2002_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Xu_et.al._2002-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-Jaime_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Jaime-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> This updated version is also based on a more complete fossil specimen exhibited at Tianjin Natural History Museum.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TNHM_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TNHM-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<p>As no feathers from <i>Sinovenator</i> have been described, the restored plumage is mostly a guess. The brownish colour is inspired from modern Phasianid birds (in which the females are usually speckled in brown nuances for camouflage), while the colour pattern is inspired by that of <i>Anchiornis</i>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Li_et.al._2010_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Li_et.al._2010-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> While the more basal <i>Anchiornis</i> had long pennacous feathers on its legs forming an extra pair of wings, <i>Sinovenator</i> is here restored without them (See Gee for speculation regarding loss of \"hind wings\").<sup id=\"cite_ref-Gee2003_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Gee2003-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> While the plumage of <i>Anchiornis</i> were quite extensive with feathers all the way down to the toes like in the modern rock ptarmigan (<i>Lagopus muta</i>), <i>Sinovenator</i> is here restored with feathers reaching down to the metatarsus like in the capercalie (<i>Tetrao urogallus</i>).\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-Xu_et.al._2002-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Xu_et.al._2002_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/415780a\">[1]</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Jaime-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Jaime_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinovenator_changii_headden.gif\" title=\"File:Sinovenator changii headden.gif\">Holotype skeletal diagram</a> by Jaime Headden</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-TNHM-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-TNHM_3-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinovenator-Tianjin_Natural_History_Museum.jpg\" title=\"File:Sinovenator-Tianjin Natural History Museum.jpg\">File:Sinovenator-Tianjin Natural History Museum.jpg</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Li_et.al._2010-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Li_et.al._2010_4-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://doc.rero.ch/record/210394/files/PAL_E4402.pdf\">[2]</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Gee2003-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Gee2003_5-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.nature.com/news/2003/030120/full/news030120-7.html\">[3]</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
